Package: marklens
Version: @VERSION@
Section: text
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: @DEPENDS@
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Homepage: https://github.com/poli0981/MarkLens
Description: fast, lightweight, read-only Markdown viewer
 MarkLens opens .md and .mdx files, or whole folders, and renders them
 faithfully - nothing more. It is a viewer the way SumatraPDF is a viewer:
 instant to open, it remembers where you were, and it never writes to your
 documents.
 .
 GitHub-flavoured Markdown with syntax-highlighted code blocks, SVG images and
 a YAML front-matter panel. Sidebar, tabs and a quick switcher; an outline
 panel; find in file and across open files; auto-reload when a document changes
 on disk; light and dark themes; and an English, Vietnamese or Japanese
 interface.
 .
 MDX components and embedded HTML are displayed as inert placeholders. There is
 no JavaScript engine, no webview and no telemetry. The only network traffic is
 an update check against GitHub Releases, at most once a day - on by default,
 and off with one setting - and remote images, which are off by default.
